(1) modulus-covariance: g_n(a,b)=(n/2)*ab*K^(n)(a,b) stable for n>=2*max(speed)?
   n= 7: g = [1, 1, 2, 1, 3, 1, 2, 4, 6, 1, 9, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12]
   n=14: g = [1, 1, 2, 1, 3, 1, 2, 3, 4, 1, 5, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
   n=28: g = [1, 1, 2, 1, 3, 1, 2, 3, 4, 1, 5, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
   n=56: g = [1, 1, 2, 1, 3, 1, 2, 3, 4, 1, 5, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
   -> n=14,28,56 identical (stable); n=7 deviates (apex too small => wide-tooth over-overlap).

(2) Eisenstein fold K^(2n)/K^(n) = 1/2 (pure rescale), EXCEPT at the apex:
   (1,3): K^7/K^14=    2  K^14/K^28=    2
   (2,3): K^7/K^14=    2  K^14/K^28=    2
   (3,5): K^7/K^14=  8/3  K^14/K^28=    2  <-- apex break
   (2,5): K^7/K^14=    2  K^14/K^28=    2
   (4,7): K^7/K^14=    4  K^14/K^28=    2  <-- apex break
   (5,8): K^7/K^14= 22/5  K^14/K^28=    2  <-- apex break

(3) the break is at speeds > n/2 = 7: antipode half (speeds 8..13) deviates at n=14.
    speeds<=7: K^(14)=(1/7)h (clean three-gap); speeds 8..13: K(a,13)=(2a-1)/(91a) deviates.
      K^14(a=6,13)= 11/546   (2a-1)/(91a)=11/546
      K^14(a=7,13)= 1/49   (2a-1)/(91a)=1/49
      K^14(a=8,13)= 15/728   (2a-1)/(91a)=15/728
    => the three recursions (Mobius order / Eisenstein modulus / Legendre three-gap) concentrate
       at the apex 7 = n/2; the antipode-half deviation is the entire LRC(14) difficulty.
